WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.190 --> 00:00:05.160
When I first reviewed the 2018 iPad Pro, I
concluded that it was not a computer replacement

00:00:05.160 --> 00:00:07.570
liked Apple’s famous “What’s a computer”
ad claimed.

00:00:07.570 --> 00:00:12.019
I mentioned that it won’t replace a laptop
until Apple wanted it to, and after spend

00:00:12.019 --> 00:00:17.040
two weeks with Apple’s brand new iPadOS,
which is completely separate from iOS, I can

00:00:17.040 --> 00:00:20.940
tell you now that you can legitimately replace
your laptop with the new iPad Pro.

00:00:20.940 --> 00:00:25.380
Before we get into those changes, let me give
you a quick rundown on what makes the 2018

00:00:25.380 --> 00:00:27.110
iPad Pro stand out from the crowd.

00:00:27.110 --> 00:00:31.820
It’s the first iPad ever to pack a rounded
display that makes it look unique and modern.

00:00:31.820 --> 00:00:35.949
It’s the first iPad ever to have no visible
form of authentication.

00:00:35.949 --> 00:00:40.690
Touch ID is gone and there’s no notch for
Face ID, so it seems to unlock magically,

00:00:40.690 --> 00:00:42.129
even while it’s upside down.

00:00:42.129 --> 00:00:46.170
The new straight-edged design is completely
unique, made to support wireless charging

00:00:46.170 --> 00:00:51.220
on the newly updated Apple Pencil, which holds
onto the iPad Pro magnetically for storage,

00:00:51.220 --> 00:00:54.760
and packs a new double-tap feature that greatly
boosts productivity.

00:00:54.760 --> 00:00:58.389
The new smart keyboard folio is perfectly
sleek and makes it feel like you’re using

00:00:58.389 --> 00:01:02.499
a laptop, and if you don’t like it, there
are awesome alternatives from Brydge and Logitech

00:01:02.499 --> 00:01:03.879
that work very well.

00:01:03.879 --> 00:01:08.260
It packs four high-quality speakers that make
the rest of the iPad lineup sound like Android

00:01:08.260 --> 00:01:12.030
tablets, and the display feels buttery smooth
with the ProMotion 120hz technology.

00:01:12.030 --> 00:01:17.290
For the downsides, the headphone jack is now
gone, but it’s not a big deal since USB-C

00:01:17.290 --> 00:01:19.170
adapters are so cheap on Amazon.

00:01:19.170 --> 00:01:24.570
It’s also expensive, starting at $800, but
now that iPadOS is coming, we definitely think

00:01:24.570 --> 00:01:29.920
it’s worth it over the other iPads, especially
at Amazon’s sale price of just $700, and

00:01:29.920 --> 00:01:33.340
if you’re like me and you wanna make sure
