00:02:05.600 --> 00:02:10.320
So back to the iPad Pro, let’s discuss the
awesome new changes coming with iPadOS that

00:02:10.320 --> 00:02:12.160
allow you to replace your laptop.

00:02:12.160 --> 00:02:15.660
First off, getting USB-C on this iPad Pro
didn’t really mean much since it was so

00:02:15.660 --> 00:02:20.590
limited, not allowing you to connect external
drives, but we now finally have external storage

00:02:20.590 --> 00:02:22.310
support that works really well!

00:02:22.310 --> 00:02:26.880
You can connect anything from a flash drive
to a hard drive or SD card, and transfer various

00:02:26.880 --> 00:02:29.510
types of files to the iPad's local storage
folder.

00:02:29.510 --> 00:02:33.480
You can even connect multiple drives at once
and transfer files between them.

00:02:33.480 --> 00:02:38.090
You can zip and unzip files and folders, And
if you use split-view, you can drag and drop

00:02:38.090 --> 00:02:42.230
files directly from a hard drive to an app
like Lumafusion, and it’ll all work without

00:02:42.230 --> 00:02:45.650
importing the file to camera roll or the iPad’s
local storage.

00:02:45.650 --> 00:02:48.920
We have a full guide to external storage,
which we’ll link to at the end of this video.

00:02:48.920 --> 00:02:53.920
Now there’s actually a big list of iPads
that support iPadOS, but the 2018 iPad Pro

00:02:53.920 --> 00:02:57.319
and it’s USB-C port is the way to go for
external storage support.

00:02:57.319 --> 00:03:01.970
The old Lightning port isn’t able to supply
enough power to be able to drive various storage

00:03:01.970 --> 00:03:06.630
drives, so it requires a special camera kit
adapter, which plugs into power, and even

00:03:06.630 --> 00:03:08.770
then, some drives still won’t work.

00:03:08.770 --> 00:03:12.160
So the convenience of USB-C is well worth
it on the iPad Pro.

00:03:12.160 --> 00:03:16.880
One thing that’s pretty amazing is SMB server
support, which works incredibly well, allowing

00:03:16.880 --> 00:03:21.290
you to connect to hard drives or servers over
a WiFi connection so you can view and transfer

00:03:21.290 --> 00:03:22.750
your archived files.

00:03:22.750 --> 00:03:28.010
With iPadOS, you can now open multiple instances
of the same app in split-view, like two notes

00:03:28.010 --> 00:03:33.180
apps or two Files apps to make transferring
files easier, and it even works with third-party

00:03:33.180 --> 00:03:34.260
apps that support it.

00:03:34.260 --> 00:03:38.260
There’s also a bunch of new multitasking
features and gestures that make the iPad much

00:03:38.260 --> 00:03:43.880
easier to use, like easier ways to select
text and finally an undo gesture that doesn’t

00:03:43.880 --> 00:03:45.290
require you to shake your iPad.

00:03:45.290 --> 00:03:49.520
Safari has seen some awesome new updates like
automatic desktop mode that’s optimized

00:03:49.520 --> 00:03:53.480
for touch, and there’s a new download manager,
similar to what you get on Mac.

00:03:53.480 --> 00:03:57.879
In the settings, you can easily change the
download location to wherever you want.

00:03:57.879 --> 00:04:02.370
We were even able to download a powerpoint
file from google and edit it using Keynote.

00:04:02.370 --> 00:04:06.959
Perhaps the best part is that iPadOS is getting
exactly the same physical keyboard shortcuts

00:04:06.959 --> 00:04:11.690
that we’re used to on macOS, both for use
within Safari and basically everywhere else

00:04:11.690 --> 00:04:13.970
on the iPad, so making the switch is much
easier.

00:04:13.970 --> 00:04:17.720
And if you’re using the onscreen keyboard,
you’ll be able to pinch it to shrink it

00:04:17.720 --> 00:04:21.739
down and move it anywhere you’d like, as
well as use the new swipe keyboard which works

00:04:21.739 --> 00:04:22.739
incredibly well.

00:04:22.739 --> 00:04:26.910
It’s even better for Apple Pencil users
since input latency has been reduced from

00:04:26.910 --> 00:04:31.250
an industry-leading 20ms to a very impressive
9ms.

00:04:31.250 --> 00:04:35.211
There’s a new tool palette which can be
easily moved around so it doesn’t get in

00:04:35.211 --> 00:04:39.490
your way, and it’s much easier to mark up
a page, just drag from the corner of the screen

00:04:39.490 --> 00:04:41.060
using the apple pencil.

00:04:41.060 --> 00:04:45.100
From here, you can mark it up and share it,
or tap the Full Page button at the top to

00:04:45.100 --> 00:04:47.120
be able to scroll through the entire page.

00:04:47.120 --> 00:04:51.050
And you can even grab the scroll bar and scroll
up and down without having to swipe.

00:04:51.050 --> 00:04:55.530
And it doesn’t stop there, Apple has finally
added Bluetooth mouse support, but you don’t

00:04:55.530 --> 00:04:59.270
actually get a cursor like you do on a Mac,
you’re basically just moving your finger

00:04:59.270 --> 00:05:03.560
around and clicking the mouse to perform a
touch gesture, so it’s not the best solution

00:05:03.560 --> 00:05:07.440
However, it does fix a huge issue with external
monitor mirroring.

00:05:07.440 --> 00:05:12.350
Before, if you use an external display, you’d
still have to touch the iPad to navigate,

00:05:12.350 --> 00:05:16.220
but now, you can use a Bluetooth mouse and
keyboard and set your iPad to the side.

00:05:16.220 --> 00:05:20.370
Not only that, but if you have a Mac running
macOS Catalina, you can use the iPad as a

00:05:20.370 --> 00:05:25.560
secondary display to do things like wirelessly
draw directly into the full macOS photoshop

00:05:25.560 --> 00:05:27.160
app using the iPad.

00:05:27.160 --> 00:05:31.610
On top of that, the iPad Pro outperforms the
rest of Apple’s latest iPad lineup by a

00:05:31.610 --> 00:05:35.740
massive margin, so you’re gonna have no
performance issues in basically any app or

00:05:35.740 --> 00:05:36.740
game out there.

00:05:36.740 --> 00:05:41.440
I previously stated that people should just
buy the 2019 iPad Air because the iPad Pro’s

00:05:41.440 --> 00:05:45.169
performance was so limited due to software,
but I’ve completely changed my mind now

00:05:45.169 --> 00:05:47.030
that iPadOS is coming out.

00:05:47.030 --> 00:05:51.440
Having USB-C and this level of performance
guarantees the best possible support for apps

00:05:51.440 --> 00:05:56.360
and features for years to come, and the unique
design, awesome quad-speakers and new Apple

00:05:56.360 --> 00:05:59.330
Pencil make it feel unique and special compared
to the other iPads.

00:05:59.330 --> 00:06:04.720
I’d have to say that paying only $700 with
Prime shipping for this iPad Pro, or even

00:06:04.720 --> 00:06:09.880
$900 for the 256GB model is well worth the
price, especially if you’re trying to replace

00:06:09.880 --> 00:06:11.190
a much more expensive laptop.

00:06:11.190 --> 00:06:15.460
I’d definitely recommend anyone looking
at the 2019 iPad Air to just save some more

00:06:15.460 --> 00:06:19.919
cash and go for the iPad Pro, because with
iPadOS, it’s finally become what Apple has

00:06:19.919 --> 00:06:21.140
envisioned it to be.

00:06:21.140 --> 00:06:24.850
If you enjoyed this long-term review, make
sure to hit that like button, click the circle

00:06:24.850 --> 00:06:27.880
above to subscribe, and check out one of those
two videos right there.

00:06:27.880 --> 00:06:33.330
Thanks for watching, and we’ll see you in
